=== WHAT WAS BUILT (parity with the web source, read end-to-end) ===
  FleetSummary is the fleet headline-stats strip of the Vehicles page. The native
  surface reproduces its data, composition, every state, and i18n keys via shared
  P1/S8 state-holder seams (no view I/O):

  Composition (web → native):
   - Four glass stat tiles in a 2-col→4-col responsive grid (web
     `grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4`), each a TSGlassPanel with a centered tinted
     SF Symbol + an animated value (TSAnimatedNumber, web `AnimatedNumber`) + an
     uppercase muted label:
       1. Vehicles      — web `vehicles.length`                (car.fill, cyan)
       2. Avg Battery   — web `round(sum(battery_level)/n)`%   (battery.100, green)
       3. Total Range   — web `round(convertDistanceFromSI(Σrated_range, distance))`
                          with the unit on the label            (gauge.medium, purple)
       4. Charging/Online — web `chargingCount` / `onlineCount` (bolt.fill, amber;
                          value tinted green per web `text-green-500`)
   - The aggregation pipeline is reproduced VERBATIM: resolved-states filter
     (web `(allStates ?? []).filter(s => s != null)`), average battery over resolved
     states only (0 when none), Σ rated_range in SI metres → convertDistanceFromSI at
     the render boundary (web useUnits), is_charging count, online = resolved count.
   - Number formatting ports web `fmtNumber` (grouped, locale-aware, half-up); SI
     distance ports web `convertDistanceFromSI` (km/mi/ft; METERS_PER_KM/MILE/FOOT
     byte-identical).

  Seams (P1/S8): FleetSummarySource (vehicle list + per-vehicle state stream + refresh)
    → FleetSummaryModel (@Observable). Previews/tests inject InMemoryFleetSummarySource;
    the view performs no networking. Telemetry (P1/S11): view.opened with surface slug
    "FleetSummary", emitted once. i18n (P1/S10): every string via FleetSummaryStrings;
    0 hardcoded English literals in native code.

